{"id":"mahabharata-13-076","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":76,"title":"षट्सप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 76 · The greatness of cows continued","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks for more on the merit of giving cows, and Bhishma tells how cows are the source of the world's livelihood, as the gods live on nectar. He tells how the cows, rising from the ocean of nectar as Moon's brightness flows, give milk, and how King Saudasa gave a thousand cows to brahmins and won the worlds.","kn":"ಗೋದಾನದ ಪುಣ್ಯದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ಹೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದೇವತೆಗಳು ಅಮೃತದಲ್ಲಿ ಬದುಕುವಂತೆ ಗೋವುಗಳು ಲೋಕದ ಜೀವನಾಧಾರ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಮೃತದಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ರೋಹಿಣಿ ಗೋವುಗಳು ಹಾಲು ಸುರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ, ಸೌದಾಸ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರಿಗೆ ಸಾವಿರಾರು ಗೋದಾನ ಮಾಡಿ ಲೋಕ ಗೆದ್ದ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर गोदान के पुण्य पर और पूछते हैं, और भीष्म कहते हैं कि जैसे देवता अमृत पर जीते हैं वैसे गौएँ संसार की आजीविका हैं। वे बताते हैं कि अमृत से उपजी रोहिणी गौएँ दूध देती हैं और सौदास ने ब्राह्मणों को हजारों गौएँ देकर लोक जीते।","te":"గోదాన పుణ్యం గురించి మరింత చెప్పమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; దేవతలు అమృతంతో జీవించినట్లు ఆవులు లోక జీవనాధారమని భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. అమృతం నుండి పుట్టిన రోహిణి ఆవులు పాలిస్తాయని, సౌదాసుడు బ్రాహ్మణులకు వేల ఆవులిచ్చి లోకాలు గెలిచాడని అంటాడు.","ta":"பசுதான புண்ணியம் பற்றி மேலும் கூறுமாறு யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, தேவர் அமுதத்தால் வாழ்வது போல் பசுக்கள் உலகின் வாழ்வாதாரம் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். அமுதத்தில் தோன்றிய ரோகிணி பசுக்கள் பால் சொரிகின்றன, சௌதாசன் அந்தணருக்கு ஆயிரக்கணக்கான பசுக்களைத் தந்து உலகங்களை வென்றான் என்கிறார்.","ml":"പശുദാനത്തിന്റെ പുണ്യത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് കൂടുതൽ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; പശുക്കളിൽനിന്നാണ് ലോകത്തിന്റെ ജീവനോപാധി, ദേവന്മാർ അമൃതുണ്ടു ജീവിക്കുന്നതുപോലെ എന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. അമൃതസമുദ്രത്തിൽനിന്ന് ഉയർന്ന പശുക്കൾ, ചന്ദ്രപ്രകാശം ഒഴുകുമ്പോൾ പാൽ ചുരത്തുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും, സൗദാസ രാജാവ് ബ്രാഹ്മണർക്ക് ആയിരം പശുക്കളെ നൽകി ലോകങ്ങൾ നേടിയതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.76; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा भूयः शांतनवं नृप ।\nगोदाने विस्तरं धीमान्पप्रच्छ विनयान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, wise and humble, again asked Bhishma, son of Shantanu, to explain at length the gift of cows."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"गोप्रदाने गुणान्सम्यक्पुनः प्रब्रूहि भारत ।\nन हि तृप्याम्यहं वीर शृण्वानोऽमृतमीदृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Bharata, tell me again the true merits of giving cows. Hero, I am never satisfied hearing such nectar."}},{"n":3,"text":"इत्युक्तो धर्मराजेन तदा शांतनवो नृप ।\nसम्यगाह गुणांस्तस्मै गोप्रदानस्य केवलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the king of dharma, Bhishma, son of Shantanu, then explained to him fully the merits of the cow-gift alone."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"वत्सलां गुणसंपन्नां तरुणीं वस्त्रसंवृताम् ।\nदत्त्वेदृशीं गां विप्राय सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a brahmin a cow of this kind, affectionate, well-endowed, young and covered with cloth, is freed from all sins."}},{"n":5,"text":"असुर्या नाम ते लोका गां दत्त्वा तत्र गच्छति ।\nपीतोदकां जग्धतृणां नष्टदुग्धां निरिन्द्रियाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a cow that has already drunk her water, eaten her grass, has gone dry and is weak in her senses goes to the worlds called Asurya."}},{"n":6,"text":"जरोग्रामुपयुक्तार्थां जीर्णां कूपमिवाजलम् ।\nदत्त्वा तमः प्रविशति द्विजं क्लेशेन योजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A cow that is old, fierce, already used up, worn out like a waterless well: giving such a cow, he enters darkness, for he has only burdened the brahmin with trouble."}},{"n":7,"text":"दुष्टा रुष्टा व्याधिता दुर्बला वा\nन दातव्या याश्च मूल्यैरदत्तैः ।\nक्लेशैर्विप्रं योऽफलैः संयुनक्ति\nतस्यावीर्याश्चाफलाश्चैव लोकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cows that are vicious, angry, sick or weak, or that are to be had without payment of their price, should not be given. One who burdens a brahmin with such fruitless troubles gains worlds that are powerless and fruitless."}},{"n":8,"text":"बलान्विताः शीलवयोपपन्नाः\nसर्वाः प्रशंसन्ति सुगन्धवत्यः ।\nयथा हि गङ्गा सरितां वरिष्ठा\nतथार्जुनीनां कपिला वरिष्ठा ॥","meaning":{"en":"All cows that are strong, gentle, young and sweet-smelling are praised. As the Ganga is the best of rivers, so the tawny cow is the best among the white-marked cows."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"कस्मात्समाने बहुलाप्रदाने\nसद्भिः प्रशस्तं कपिलाप्रदानम् ।\nविशेषमिच्छामि महानुभाव\nश्रोतुं समर्थो हि भवान्प्रवक्तुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why, when the giving of a cow of any kind is equal, do the good praise the gift of a tawny cow? Noble one, I wish to hear the distinction; you are able to tell it."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"वृद्धानां ब्रुवतां तात श्रुतं मे यत्प्रभाषसे ।\nवक्ष्यामि तदशेषेण रोहिण्यो निर्मिता यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear child, what you say agrees with what I heard from the elders. I shall tell it entire, how the Rohini cows were made."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रजाः सृजेति व्यादिष्टः पूर्वं दक्षः स्वयंभुवा ।\nअसृजद्वृत्तिमेवाग्रे प्रजानां हितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago Daksha, told by the self-born Brahma to create beings, first created livelihood, wishing the good of creatures."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथा ह्यमृतमाश्रित्य वर्तयन्ति दिवौकसः ।\nतथा वृत्तिं समाश्रित्य वर्तयन्ति प्रजा विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"O lord, as the gods live by relying on nectar, so creatures live by relying on a means of livelihood."}},{"n":13,"text":"अचरेभ्यश्च भूतेभ्यश्चराः श्रेष्ठास्ततो नराः ।\nब्राह्मणाश्च ततः श्रेष्ठास्तेषु यज्ञाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among beings, moving ones are better than unmoving; among them men are better; among them brahmins are better, and in them sacrifices are established."}},{"n":14,"text":"यज्ञैराप्यायते सोमः स च गोषु प्रतिष्ठितः ।\nसर्वे देवाः प्रमोदन्ते पूर्ववृत्तास्ततः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By sacrifices Soma is nourished, and he is established in the cows. All the gods rejoice, and creatures live by what came before."}},{"n":15,"text":"एतान्येव तु भूतानि प्राक्रोशन्वृत्तिकाङ्क्षया ।\nवृत्तिदं चान्वपद्यन्त तृषिताः पितृमातृवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These very beings cried out in wanting livelihood, and thirsty, they went to the giver of livelihood as to a father and mother."}},{"n":16,"text":"इतीदं मनसा गत्वा प्रजासर्गार्थमात्मनः ।\nप्रजापतिर्बलाधानममृतं प्रापिबत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking thus in his mind about making creatures, Prajapati then drank nectar to place strength in himself."}},{"n":17,"text":"स गतस्तस्य तृप्तिं तु गन्धं सुरभिमुद्गिरन् ।\nददर्शोद्गारसंवृत्तां सुरभिं मुखजां सुताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satisfied, he breathed out a sweet fragrance, and in that breath he saw Surabhi, a daughter born from his mouth."}},{"n":18,"text":"सासृजत्सौरभेयीस्तु सुरभिर्लोकमातरः ।\nसुवर्णवर्णाः कपिलाः प्रजानां वृत्तिधेनवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surabhi created the Saurabheyi cows, mothers of the world, golden-hued and tawny, the cows that give creatures their livelihood."}},{"n":19,"text":"तासाममृतवर्णानां क्षरन्तीनां समन्ततः ।\nबभूवामृतजः फेनः स्रवन्तीनामिवोर्मिजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those nectar-coloured cows flowed all around, a foam born of nectar arose, like waves from flowing rivers."}},{"n":20,"text":"स वत्समुखविभ्रष्टो भवस्य भुवि तिष्ठतः ।\nशिरस्यवाप तत्क्रुद्धः स तदोदैक्षत प्रभुः ।\nललाटप्रभवेनाक्ष्णा रोहिणीः प्रदहन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"That foam slipped from a calf's mouth and fell on the head of Bhava, who stood on the earth. Angry, the lord looked with the eye born in his forehead, as if burning the Rohini cows."}},{"n":21,"text":"तत्तेजस्तु ततो रौद्रं कपिला गा विशां पते ।\nनानावर्णत्वमनयन्मेघानिव दिवाकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O lord of the people, that fierce fire-energy turned the tawny cows to many colours, as the sun does to clouds."}},{"n":22,"text":"यास्तु तस्मादपक्रम्य सोममेवाभिसंश्रिताः ।\nयथोत्पन्नाः स्ववर्णस्थास्ता नीता नान्यवर्णताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those that moved away from it and sheltered with Soma stayed in their own colour as they were born, and were not changed to another colour."}},{"n":23,"text":"अथ क्रुद्धं महादेवं प्रजापतिरभाषत ।\nअमृतेनावसिक्तस्त्वं नोच्छिष्टं विद्यते गवाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Prajapati said to the angry Mahadeva, 'You were sprinkled with nectar; there is no impurity in cows."}},{"n":24,"text":"यथा ह्यमृतमादाय सोमो विष्यन्दते पुनः ।\nतथा क्षीरं क्षरन्त्येता रोहिण्योऽमृतसंभवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Soma takes up nectar and flows again, so these Rohinis, born of nectar, let milk flow."}},{"n":25,"text":"न दुष्यत्यनिलो नाग्निर्न सुवर्णं न चोदधिः ।\nनामृतेनामृतं पीतं वत्सपीता न वत्सला ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wind is not defiled, nor fire, nor gold, nor the ocean; nectar drunk by nectar is no fault, and a cow suckled by her calf is not spoiled."}},{"n":26,"text":"इमाँल्लोकान्भरिष्यन्ति हविषा प्रस्नवेन च ।\nआसामैश्वर्यमश्नीहि सर्वामृतमयं शुभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With oblations and with their milk they will sustain these worlds. Take lordship over them, auspicious and made wholly of nectar.'"}},{"n":27,"text":"वृषभं च ददौ तस्मै सह ताभिः प्रजापतिः ।\nप्रसादयामास मनस्तेन रुद्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prajapati gave him a bull along with those cows, O Bharata, and so appeased the mind of Rudra."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रीतश्चापि महादेवश्चकार वृषभं तदा ।\nध्वजं च वाहनं चैव तस्मात्स वृषभध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahadeva, pleased, made the bull his banner and his vehicle; therefore he is called the one with the bull for banner."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो देवैर्महादेवस्तदा पशुपतिः कृतः ।\nईश्वरः स गवां मध्ये वृषाङ्क इति चोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the gods made Mahadeva the lord of cattle. As the lord among the cows he is called the one marked with the bull."}},{"n":30,"text":"एवमव्यग्रवर्णानां कपिलानां महौजसाम् ।\nप्रदाने प्रथमः कल्पः सर्वासामेव कीर्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the first rule of giving is declared for all tawny cows, of unshaken colour and great vigour."}},{"n":31,"text":"लोकज्येष्ठा लोकवृत्तिप्रवृत्ता\nरुद्रोपेताः सोमविष्यन्दभूताः ।\nसौम्याः पुण्याः कामदाः प्राणदाश्च\nगा वै दत्त्वा सर्वकामप्रदः स्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eldest in the world, engaged in sustaining the world, joined with Rudra, born of Soma's flow, gentle, holy, granting wishes and life: one who gives such cows becomes a giver of all desires."}},{"n":32,"text":"इमं गवां प्रभवविधानमुत्तमं\nपठन्सदा शुचिरतिमङ्गलप्रियः ।\nविमुच्यते कलिकलुषेण मानवः\nप्रियं सुतान्पशुधनमाप्नुयात्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, pure and fond of auspicious things, always reads this supreme account of the origin of cows is freed from the taint of the Kali age, and gains what he loves, sons and cattle."}},{"n":33,"text":"हव्यं कव्यं तर्पणं शान्तिकर्म\nयानं वासो वृद्धबालस्य पुष्टिम् ।\nएतान्सर्वान्गोप्रदाने गुणान्वै\nदाता राजन्नाप्नुयाद्वै सदैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Offerings to gods and ancestors, satisfying them, rites of peace, vehicles, clothing, and nourishment for the old and the young: the giver of a cow, O king, always gains all these merits."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":34,"text":"पितामहस्याथ निशम्य वाक्यं\nराजा सह भ्रातृभिराजमीढः ।\nसौवर्णकांस्योपदुहास्ततो गाः\nपार्थो ददौ ब्राह्मणसत्तमेभ्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the grandsire's words, the king, Yudhishthira of the Ajamidha line, with his brothers, gave cows with gold and bronze milk pails to the best of brahmins."}},{"n":35,"text":"तथैव तेभ्योऽभिददौ द्विजेभ्यो\nगवां सहस्राणि शतानि चैव ।\nयज्ञान्समुद्दिश्य च दक्षिणार्थे\nलोकान्विजेतुं परमां च कीर्तिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too he gave those brahmins hundreds and thousands of cows, intending them as sacrificial fees for his sacrifices, to win the worlds and supreme fame."}}]}]}